* A mistake in the data. JOSS stops at the step that cannot be done and
* says why. The value is put right, and Go takes up the work where it
* stopped: nothing is done twice and nothing is lost.
1.1 Set s = s + sqrt[x(i)].
1.2 Type i, x(i), s in form 1.
Form 1:
__   x = ___   sum of roots so far ___.____

Set x(1) = 4.
Set x(2) = 9.
Set x(3) = -16.
Set x(4) = 25.
Set s = 0.
Do part 1 for i = 1(1)4.
Type i, x(i).
Set x(3) = 16.
Go.
